From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Combray <combray@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Net: persist cookies on request and write profile files
 atomically

Servo writes the cookie jar, HSTS list and HTTP auth cache only when
the resource thread exits. Android kills background apps without a
clean shutdown, so every login since the last exit was lost.

Add CoreResourceMsg::PersistState and SiteDataManager::persist_to_disk
so an embedder can write the same state at any time, for example when
the app goes to the background. It reports whether every file was
written.

Profile files (also localStorage) were written in place: a kill during
the write left a truncated file, and a failed create panicked the
writing thread. Write a temporary file and rename it over the old one,
and log write failures instead of panicking.
